-- ``enabled``: This option is enabled by default. When enabled, you can access the metrics through the ``metrics`` endpoint of a BentoML Service.
+- ``enabled``: This option is enabled by default. When enabled, you can access the metrics through the ``metrics`` endpoint of a BentoML Service. When disabled, the ``/metrics`` route is not registered at all.
 - ``namespace``: Follows the `labeling convention <https://prometheus.io/docs/practices/naming/#metric-and-label-naming>`_ of Prometheus. The default namespace is ``bentoml_service``, which covers most use cases.
 
+Add custom metric lines
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+
+To inject additional metric lines into the ``/metrics`` response, define a ``__metrics__`` method on your Service class. It receives the raw Prometheus metrics text and must return a (possibly modified) string:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    @bentoml.service
+    class MyService:
+        def __metrics__(self, metrics_text: str) -> str:
+            return metrics_text + '\nmy_custom_metric 1\n'
+
+This is useful for exposing metrics produced by your own code alongside the default BentoML metrics.
+
